{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b3e3auk9f","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qsqgr7rLjEk9dYMk1tjuUn","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run2-repo/7ffcf238-91d1-4f12-ba72-3238a3e8c8e2/tasks/b3e3auk9f.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_2\ncat > $D/model_name.txt << 'EOF'\nalignable_difference_comparison\nEOF\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nPeople compare the two sequences by aligning them flip by flip (structural alignment), and how sharply they act on their impression of which looks more random depends on how alignable the pair is: when the two strings share most of their flips position by position, the few places where they differ stand out and the comparison is decided by them sharply, whereas when the strings differ almost everywhere the comparison is holistic and close to a guess (or, if alignment hurts, the reverse — the direction is a single shared parameter). The impression itself is the current best model's (tally span against a personal expected span, switching against a personal ideal rate, chunk variety and a rule-built penalty scaled by personal pattern sensitivity, a penalty on a terminal streak, a personal left/right lean that is not scaled); the claim is the shared dependence of decisiveness on the pair's position-by-position dissimilarity, so the same felt difference in randomness yields stronger consensus for a near-identical pair than for a pair of unrelated strings.\nEOF\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc=open('/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule.py').read()\ndoc='''\"\"\"Alignable-difference comparison: decisiveness depends on how alignable the pair is.\n\nPeople compare the two sequences by aligning them flip by flip; how sharply\nthey act on their impression of which looks more random depends on the share of\npositions at which the two strings differ (a shared exponential gain, direction\nfree). The impression is the current best model's (tally span against a personal\nexpected span, switching against a personal ideal rate, chunk variety and a\nrule-built penalty scaled by personal pattern sensitivity, a terminal-streak\npenalty); the personal left/right lean is not scaled.\n\"\"\"'''\ni=src.index('import numpy')\nsrc=doc+'\\n'+src[i:]\nsrc=src.replace('''        \"log_len\": float(np.log(len(a) / 6.0)),''','''        \"log_len\": float(np.log(len(a) / 6.0)),\n        # Share of aligned positions at which the two strings differ, centred.\n        \"mismatch\": float(np.mean([x != y for x, y in zip(a, b)])) - 0.5,''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    log_len = pm.Data(\"log_len\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))''','''    log_len = pm.Data(\"log_len\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    mismatch = pm.Data(\"mismatch\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    # Person-specific left/right''','''    # The claim: decisiveness scales with the pair's position-wise dissimilarity.\n    delta = pm.Normal(\"delta\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.5)\n    gain = pm.math.exp(delta * mismatch)\n\n    # Person-specific left/right''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    logit = (\n        sens''','''    impression = (\n        sens''')\nsrc=src.replace('''        - tau * term_diff\n        + side[participant_id]\n    )''','''        - tau * term_diff\n    )\n    logit = gain * impression + side[participant_id]''')\nopen('/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_2/candidate.py','w').write(src)\nPY\ngrep -n \"gain\\|mismatch\\|impression\\|logit\" $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"70d2a94f-8021-4151-8908-4cf06c61935f","session_id":"7ffcf238-91d1-4f12-ba72-3238a3e8c8e2"}
