{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfh1F854a1cS6X2N3Sthm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote all three files for candidate 2, and the self-check printed `OK`.\n\n**Model name:** `alignable_difference_comparison`\n\n**Hypothesis:** People compare the two sequences by lining them up flip by flip. How firmly they act on their sense of which one looks more random depends on how alike the two strings are, measured as the share of positions where they differ. When two strings match in most positions, the few differences stand out, so the same gap in perceived randomness could produce a stronger consensus. When they differ almost everywhere, the comparison is more of a guess. One shared parameter sets which way this goes and how strongly. This is a rule about how the pair is compared, not a new cue.\n\n**Implementation:** It uses the current best model's judgement of each sequence unchanged (`terminal_streak_recency_pattern_rule`). That judgement is multiplied by `exp(delta · (mismatch − 0.5))`, where `mismatch` is the share of positions at which the two strings differ. The person's left/right lean is added afterwards and is not scaled. This adds one parameter, `delta`, with a Normal(0, 1.5) prior. The 356 distinct pairs vary widely on this measure, from 12.5% to 100% of positions differing, with a median of 57%.\n\n**Check result:**\n- The score (ELPD-LOO) on the short smoke fit was −3256.2, against −3262.5 for the current best model. That smoke fit was 100 draws on one chain, so this is only a hint, not a fair comparison.\n- That fit flagged the score as unreliable: 13.9% of trials had a high Pareto k, against a 1% tolerance. The check still passes, but admission's full fit may give an untrustworthy estimate too.\n- The check couldn't verify convergence, since a single chain doesn't report R-hat.\n- The check took about 20 minutes, including compilation. The full admission fit has a 30-minute limit per sampling run, and its cost should be about the same as the current best model's, so this is a real risk.\n- The check doesn't test novelty. It's unconfirmed that the model predicts differently enough from the existing ones to pass the novelty gate.\n\nI didn't target the critique's one discrepancy, about 4-flip alternating windows. It didn't survive the false-discovery correction (q = 0.304), and adding a cue for it would have meant grafting into an exploratory slot.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_2/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2465,"cache_read_input_tokens":88816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2465,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ffcf238-91d1-4f12-ba72-3238a3e8c8e2","uuid":"94564832-81de-4983-b45c-e9c496c926ca","timestamp":"2026-10-04T10:02:34.356Z","request_id":"req_011Cfh1F78WxiJxhoiWSteti"}
